item.text:
I searched official STF, TSE, TCU, MPF, and congressional records, plus targeted scholarship on appointments. The useful recoveries are:

- A Bolsonaro-specific locator for his 2022 asset declaration.
- The official proceeding that records—and carefully limits—the allegation that Bolsonaro requested preferential MEC access.
- The TCU’s governing rule and compelled disposition of high-value official gifts.
- Important contrary evidence concerning measurable voting harm from the PRF operations and a criminal complaint over the September 7 events.
- Scholarship connecting Bolsonaro’s appointment strategy to demands for personal loyalty, although it does not establish a specific corrupt appointment in 2022.

Unresolved after repeated searches:

- I found no accessible final merits disposition for the underlying MEC corruption investigation or the separate Bolsonaro warning/leak allegation.
- I found no official final judgment approving or rejecting Bolsonaro–Braga Netto’s 2022 campaign accounts. The official extract is recoverable, but search results repeatedly returned the Lula judgment or Bolsonaro’s 2018 accounts.
- The searchable PRF records establish conduct and intent by Silvinei Vasques and other senior officials, but not a Bolsonaro order or prior notice.
- No authenticated source-of-funds or beneficial-ownership audit resolves the family real-estate questions.
- The jewelry proceedings establish public ownership rules and compelled return, but the latest located criminal proceeding still does not establish personal profit or a final merits judgment.
- No bounded example of voluntary, costly correction beyond the already-recorded legally required transition was recovered.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Candidatos 2022 — Bens de candidatos","publisher":"Tribunal Superior Eleitoral","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://dadosabertos.tse.jus.br/dataset/?_tags_limit=0&groups=candidatos&tags=Ano+2022","claim":"The TSE's official 2022 candidate-assets dataset supplies a Bolsonaro-specific declaration record rather than merely describing the disclosure system. Filtering the consolidated candidate-assets file by candidate sequence number 280001618036 identifies Jair Bolsonaro's filed asset rows, whose declared total was R$2,317,554.73. The filing is self-declared and does not authenticate acquisition history, source of funds, beneficial ownership, relatives' assets, or compatibility with income.","locator":"Dataset group 'Candidatos', election year 2022, resource 'Bens de Candidatos'; consolidated file bem_candidato_2022_BRASIL.csv; filter SQ_CANDIDATO=280001618036 and sum VR_BEM_CANDIDATO","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C2-001","canonical_fact_key":"bolsonaro_2022_tse_asset_declaration","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.4"],"source_type":"official_dataset","source_confidence":0.93,"source_confidence_reason":"Official TSE dataset with a candidate-specific stable identifier; evidentiary scope is limited because the values and descriptions are candidate declarations, not an audit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 election filing.","ruler_attribution":"The declaration was personally attributable to Bolsonaro as the registered presidential candidate, but its truth or completeness was not independently verified by the dataset.","contrary_evidence":"The public declaration weighs against saying Bolsonaro made no asset disclosure, while providing no proof that all assets or origins were fully disclosed.","underlying_fact_key":"bolsonaro_2022_tse_asset_declaration","lenses":["7B.4"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Ministra Cármen Lúcia autoriza abertura de inquérito contra o ministro da Educação","publisher":"Supremo Tribunal Federal","publication_date":"2022-03-24","url":"https://portal.stf.jus.br/noticias/verNoticiaDetalhe.asp?idConteudo=484060&ori=1","claim":"The STF opened INQ 4896 to investigate Milton Ribeiro and ordered testimony and MEC/CGU information about FNDE release criteria. The official record also states that three crime notices concerning Bolsonaro were sent to the PGR because Ribeiro allegedly said municipalities associated with Pastor Gilmar Santos were prioritized at Bolsonaro's request. This authenticates the existence and precise content of the allegation and the judicial investigative response, but is not a finding that Bolsonaro ordered bribes or particular grants.","locator":"Opening four paragraphs; INQ 4896; paragraph beginning 'A ministra também remeteu à PGR três notícias-crime'; ordered MEC and CGU clarification of the FNDE timetable and allocation criteria within 15 days","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C2-002","canonical_fact_key":"mec_pastors_bolsonaro_request_inq4896","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.5","7B.6","7B.7","7B.9"],"source_type":"official_court_record","source_confidence":0.9,"source_confidence_reason":"Official STF account of the initiating allegations and investigative order; high confidence about procedure and allegation content, but it expressly does not prove the alleged conduct.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Contemporaneous March 2022 proceeding concerning conduct in office.","ruler_attribution":"Bolsonaro is directly named in the referred crime notices, but the asserted request is attributed to Ribeiro and remained under investigation.","contrary_evidence":"The source shows institutional scrutiny was initiated promptly and does not report a merits finding against Bolsonaro.","underlying_fact_key":"mec_pastors_bolsonaro_request","lenses":["7B.5","7B.6","7B.7","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Supremo Tribunal Federal — INQ 4896 process record","publisher":"Supremo Tribunal Federal","publication_date":"2022-05","url":"https://portal.stf.jus.br/processos/detalhe.asp?incidente=6371002","claim":"After Milton Ribeiro left the ministry, the STF ceased to have original jurisdiction over the MEC investigation and remitted it to the competent federal trial court. The transfer was jurisdictional, not an acquittal, archiving on the merits, or a finding that the alleged preferential-access arrangement did not occur.","locator":"INQ 4896, incident 6371002; May 2022 decision classified as declination of jurisdiction following Ribeiro's March 28 dismissal","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C2-003","canonical_fact_key":"inq4896_jurisdiction_declination","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.6","7B.9"],"source_type":"official_docket","source_confidence":0.86,"source_confidence_reason":"Official docket identifies the proceeding and procedural transfer, but the full later first-instance history was not recoverable through the searchable interface.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct 2022 procedural response.","ruler_attribution":"No substantive culpability finding concerning Bolsonaro was made in the jurisdictional decision.","contrary_evidence":"Prevents treating the STF proceeding as a conviction or final adverse disposition.","underlying_fact_key":"inq4896_jurisdiction_declination","lenses":["7B.6","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Acórdão 443/2023 — Plenário","publisher":"Tribunal de Contas da União","publication_date":"2023-03-15","url":"https://pesquisa.apps.tcu.gov.br/doc/acordao-completo/443/2023/Plen%C3%A1rio","claim":"In proceedings over official gifts received during the Bolsonaro presidency, the TCU held that high-value personal gifts exceeded a merely symbolic diplomatic purpose and fell under the rule requiring delivery to the Union. It ordered Bolsonaro to surrender the Saudi jewelry and UAE weapons and ordered the Presidency to obtain the customs-held jewelry for incorporation into public property. The ruling resolved custody and public ownership provisionally, not criminal intent, personal profit, or the ultimate jewelry prosecution.","locator":"Acórdão 443/2023-Plenário, TC 003.679/2023-3; Sumário; operative determinations concerning delivery of the Saudi jewelry and UAE weapons; cited art. 3 of Resolução CEP/PR","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C2-004","canonical_fact_key":"bolsonaro_official_gifts_tcu_return_order","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.6","7B.8"],"source_type":"official_audit_court_decision","source_confidence":0.94,"source_confidence_reason":"Primary collegiate audit-court decision with a stable case number, governing rule, and operative remedy; it does not adjudicate criminal liability.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Later decision specifically classifying and directing disposition of gifts received because of Bolsonaro's presidency; underlying Saudi-gift event occurred in 2021 and custody extended beyond 2022.","ruler_attribution":"The order was directed personally to Bolsonaro as custodian of specified gifts received by reason of presidential office.","contrary_evidence":"Bolsonaro ultimately surrendered custody under compulsion; this is a remedy but not voluntary self-correction and does not itself prove that he profited from the gifts.","underlying_fact_key":"bolsonaro_official_gifts_disposition","lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.6","7B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Operações da PRF não resultaram em prejuízos aos eleitores, afirma presidente do TSE","publisher":"Senado Federal — Rádio Senado","publication_date":"2022-10-30","url":"https://www12.senado.leg.br/radio/1/noticia/2022/10/30/operacoes-da-prf-nao-resultaram-em-prejuizos-aos-eleitores-afirma-presidente-do-tse","claim":"On election day, TSE president Alexandre de Moraes stated that the disproportionately northeastern PRF operations had not caused measurable loss of votes. He reported that Silvinei Vasques described the stops as safety inspections of voter-transport vehicles. This is contemporaneous contrary evidence about realized electoral harm and the PRF's stated justification; it does not negate later findings that senior PRF officials acted improperly or establish that the operations were neutral in design.","locator":"Lines 29–37, especially page paragraphs immediately below the headline reporting Moraes's assessment and Vasques's explanation; October 30, 2022","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C2-005","canonical_fact_key":"prf_election_operations_no_measurable_vote_loss","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.9"],"source_type":"official_legislative_news_record","source_confidence":0.86,"source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Senate record accurately attributes the TSE president's public assessment, but it is not the underlying operational dataset or a later merits adjudication.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Same-day assessment of the October 30, 2022 operations.","ruler_attribution":"No Bolsonaro direction, notice, protection, or remedial action is attributed; the statement concerns institutional operations and their observed voting effect.","contrary_evidence":"Affirmative contrary evidence that the operations did not ultimately prevent a measurable number of votes, despite later evidence of improper targeting and partisan intent by officials.","underlying_fact_key":"prf_2022_election_operations","lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"A pedido da PGR, ministro Lewandowski arquiva pedido de investigação sobre atos de Bolsonaro no 7 de Setembro","publisher":"Supremo Tribunal Federal","publication_date":"2022-12-30","url":"https://portal.stf.jus.br/noticias/verNoticiaDetalhe.asp?idConteudo=499838&tip=UN","claim":"The STF archived PET 10576, which sought a criminal investigation of Bolsonaro for peculation and prevarication arising from his campaign-oriented September 7 speeches, because the PGR found insufficient elements and no just cause to open a criminal investigation. This does not contradict the later TSE electoral-law finding that state resources were deliberately converted to campaign use; it shows that the separate criminal theory did not clear the threshold for investigation on the evidence then presented.","locator":"Opening five paragraphs; PET 10576; section 'Titularidade da ação'; reference to CPP art. 395(III) and absence of justa causa","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C2-006","canonical_fact_key":"september7_pet10576_criminal_archiving","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.3","7B.6"],"source_type":"official_court_decision_summary","source_confidence":0.93,"source_confidence_reason":"Official STF summary clearly identifies the petition, alleged offenses, prosecutorial ground, and disposition.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Decision issued December 30, 2022 about September 2022 conduct.","ruler_attribution":"The allegations concerned Bolsonaro's own speeches and use of the presidential apparatus, but the criminal-investigation request was archived for insufficient basis.","contrary_evidence":"Strong procedural contrary evidence against describing the September 7 conduct as established peculation or prevarication; it does not displace the distinct electoral abuse judgment.","underlying_fact_key":"bolsonaro_september7_state_resources","lenses":["7B.3","7B.6"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Brazil’s Stealth Military Intervention","publisher":"GIGA Focus / SAGE Journals","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/1866802X211039860","claim":"A peer-reviewed analysis documents the unusually steep growth of military appointments to strategic managerial and advisory posts under Bolsonaro and interprets the 2021 dismissal of Defence Minister Fernando Azevedo e Silva—followed by the service commanders' resignations—as arising from resistance to Bolsonaro's increasing demands for personal loyalty. This supports a ruler-directed loyalty dimension in appointment practice, but it does not identify a corrupt quid pro quo, prove incompetence of individual 2022 appointees, or establish preferential material benefits to Bolsonaro.","locator":"Table 2 and accompanying discussion of military appointments to strategic managerial and advisory positions; section discussing the March 2021 dismissal of Azevedo e Silva and resignation of the three service commanders","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C2-007","canonical_fact_key":"bolsonaro_military_appointments_personal_loyalty","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.5"],"source_type":"peer_reviewed_scholarship","source_confidence":0.84,"source_confidence_reason":"Strong independent scholarship with quantitative appointment evidence and documented institutional events, but its loyalty interpretation is analytic and much of the decisive episode predates 2022.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Covers the Bolsonaro administration through the period leading into 2022; useful for appointment-system context rather than a discrete calendar-2022 appointment finding.","ruler_attribution":"The article directly attributes the governing appointment strategy and loyalty demands to Bolsonaro.","contrary_evidence":"The military appointees were not shown as a uniform patronage network, and the episode also demonstrates that senior officers could resist Bolsonaro rather than function as loyal dependants.","underlying_fact_key":"bolsonaro_military_appointments_personal_loyalty","lenses":["7B.5"]}
